WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.333
Hi everyone,

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:01.401
welcome to "Imseriou".

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.335
In this episode, I'm going to talk about

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.370
car modification in Taiwan.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.106
We previously filmed a large factory

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:06.906
like

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.375
DMG MORI, which is

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:09.275
a machine tool factory. Mazak

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.210
features a lot of content,

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.413
including our visits to many

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:14.981
racing pit stops

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.449
where we've seen

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.951
various manufacturers and brands

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.486
of equipment and specialized tools.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:20.387
We've also filmed

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:22.022
the glues and special tools

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.156
they use.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.791
Then, Taiwanese viewers asked me,

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.293
"You've been talking about foreign modifications

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.395
and racing

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:29.396
, why don't you talk about Taiwanese

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:32.332
modifications ?"

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:33.767
Of course, Taiwan has some amazing ones too !

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:34.968
But have you noticed anything different about

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:35.468
me today

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.369
?

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.103
Hat?

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:37.937
No,

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.105
it's my watch strap—I just

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:39.939
bought a new one!

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.241
It's so detailed!

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:42.575
Actually, I just got

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.344
my hair permed yesterday, and to avoid ruining it

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.012
, I'm not wearing a hat today.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.115
Taiwanese motorcycle modifications

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.316
actually fall into several categories

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.651
. Based on my past experience

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.119
, understanding of manufacturers

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.254
, and knowledge of the industry,

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.989
I'll break it down into several types.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.223
You can think about which level

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.725
your local motorcycle shop

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.726
belongs to.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:00.593
First, the first type, which

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.361
mostly appears in

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.495
many motorcycle shops,

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:02.962
involves things like

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:05.799
replacing

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:06.900
parts from other brands' original motorcycles with

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.968
parts from a brand you like—

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.503
like

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.605
swapping Kymco dusters for Yamaha dusters

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:13.339
, or modifying a

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:14.574
rearview mirror

00:01:14.574 --> 00:01:16.309
to something else.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.477
If the two specifications

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:18.611
are not quite the same, some

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:19.846
DIY mechanics

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.014
will use some perforated iron

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:21.781
to forcibly attach it

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:22.649
, which may

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.483
not look as good as

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:24.417
the overall proportions. A

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.852
more refined

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:28.588
mechanic will use CNC machining

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:29.456
to create a

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:31.324
matching part that looks very similar to the original

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.292
and then install it

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:33.993
. The completeness will be slightly higher.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:34.427
The second type

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:35.795
is also in modification.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:36.663
You often hear that

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.331
this brand is made by us,

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.165
and this thing

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.266
is also manufactured by us.

00:01:40.266 --> 00:01:41.401
This kind of OEM modification

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.369
actually has quite a few

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.370
small and medium-sized factories in Taiwan.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.171
So you often hear

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:45.772
a boss say, "

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:46.239
Let me tell you

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.740
, our company makes all of these.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:48.775
We calculate the price for them

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.276
, and they sell them for this much."

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:50.777
But

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.312
in fact, the drawings and designs of these things

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.680
are not done by their company.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.014
There is a brand company

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:55.815
that develops,

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:56.449
designs,

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.350
and draws a drawing,

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.119
and then entrusts other companies or factories

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.153
to

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.654
do the electroplating,

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.022
polishing, and

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.324
springs .

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:06.526
This is called this kind of OEM

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.494
modification of modification parts and modification kits.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.361
The third

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:09.496
type is more and more advanced:

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:10.797
Custom modification.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.931
For the car

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:12.765
's lines,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.134
you have your own favorite style.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.635
Some people like the supersonic style,

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.936
some ... Some people like Choppers,

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:17.637
while others prefer

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.139
various different styles.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:20.607
They take the original bike

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:22.408
and modify it

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.910
using a custom approach,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.678
sometimes including paint jobs

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.046
, or even changing the front fork

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.047
, triple clamp

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.115
, and exhaust pipe.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.150
They might even handcraft a piece of

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.918
material,

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:32.752
like a piece of wood,

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.753
and then connect it to the original. They make

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:34.821
that part

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.089
specifically for one bike,

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.090
so each bike is unique.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:37.924
Or, for an exhibition,

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:38.691
they might

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.659
order a custom-

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.194
made fairing

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.762
or use ABS panels

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.063
to create a specific shape.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.899
This kind of handcrafted customization is

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:47.967
n't uncommon in Taiwan.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:48.568
The fourth type,

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:49.435
which is becoming increasingly difficult,

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.436
is brand-based customization.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.037
For example,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.505
brand G releases a bike

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.040
, or brand K

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.008
launches a

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.242
completely new design

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.410
this season.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.945
The customization brand

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.581
will then redraw and redesign

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:02.615
the bike, even

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.450
monopolizing the entire series in the market

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.152
, launching their own brand,

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.120
mass-producing and

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.322
selling it domestically and internationally.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:10.990
This requires not only a strong sense of design

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:11.891
and aesthetics

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:14.027
, but also the ability to modify and

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.061
repair bikes

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.230
, as well as knowledge of brands and materials.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.365
This level is already considered very difficult , reaching

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.567
the level of a master craftsman.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:21.834
The previous points represent

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:22.802
the level you need to reach

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.170
. That's all considered

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:24.971
basic, something

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:25.939
you absolutely need to know.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.006
But besides that,

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:28.575
the company my friend

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:29.976
and we're visiting today

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.945
is at a higher level.

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:33.813
For example, the G

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.615
or K brand I just mentioned

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:36.716
—that's a big brand

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:37.283
, not some

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.952
random little brand.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.386
You go directly to them, saying, "

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:41.688
We've modified it so much,

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.623
can you help us create a concept car

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:44.991
?" That's level

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.092
five.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:47.961
So this is a car modification shop.

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:48.828
Don't think I'm

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:50.296
talking nonsense because

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.297
I was talking about motorcycles

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.332
and then about cars.

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:53.266
These cars

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:54.234
are just his hobby;

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:55.935
the boss himself is a race car driver, and

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.136
some of the cars in the back

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.638
are his own racing cars.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.006
This is a rare opportunity

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.074
to show you

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.141
what an FIA factory car

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:02.875
looks like

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:05.178
. Look at its internal structure,

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.012
it's quite interesting! That

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.046
's what it looks like

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.214
when it leaves the factory.

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:11.150
Wait, look at its fuel filler port, it'll be funny!

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:11.985
Without the fuel filler port

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:13.019
, doesn't the atmosphere inside feel

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:13.987
completely different?

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.054
This car is so cute when it starts,

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.022
like this.

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:21.261
Doesn't it feel like

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.428
a little boy's romantic

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.063
start-up? Let me give you a feel for it

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.336
(a little boy's happiness is so simple).

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:31.504
Do you like

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:32.639
listening to the engine sound?

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:38.144
This little hot hatch is so comfortable!

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:38.911
How do you shift gears? You press

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:40.647
the clutch

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:41.281
, pull

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:41.914
one

00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:43.816
or two. It

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:44.984
shifts gears like this.

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.387
This is the handbrake. So you see

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:48.688
how interesting

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:50.056
this owner's quirks are !

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:50.823
Do you know what this is?

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:52.692
Do you know what this is?

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:53.693
It's

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:55.061
for changing tires .

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.829
Because these cars are very aggressive,

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:57.597
minor collisions and

00:04:57.597 --> 00:05:00.600
accidents are inevitable.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.602
The seatbelts are like

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:04.103
those in a baby seat—

00:05:04.103 --> 00:05:05.438
one, two, three, four, five

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.239
straps tied together.

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:07.206
If

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.574
the driver faints or

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:09.909
the car gets damaged,

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.311
you can use this to

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.045
cut it off.

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:13.880
You know, this thing is also used to

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.981
cut cardboard boxes.

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.449
We've filmed it in a German movie;

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:17.583
it's very safe.

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.018
Later, there was a group-buying

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:20.653
promotion.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:22.055
I just mentioned the fuel tank cap

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.091
sealing—

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:25.892
it's cute, isn't it?

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:26.893
And this

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:28.394
is the boss's logo.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.263
FASS

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.497
: Because I've

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:32.565
known this boss

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:33.966
for over ten years, I want to

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.335
give you an idea of

00:05:35.335 --> 00:05:36.269
​​how meticulous this type of person can be.

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:37.136
For

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:38.338
example

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:39.238
, look at

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.239
the car he modified.

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.507
Sometimes this obsessive-compulsive disorder

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.242
is a disease that needs treatment.

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:44.644
First, look at this old car.

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:46.713
Everything you see from here in the camera view

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:48.047
is drawn and made by him.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:49.248
But I know that the average viewer

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:49.949
might not be able to tell

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.084
the difference.

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.318
Let me explain.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:53.853
It's not direct ignition,

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:54.787
right? If

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.155
a typical tuning shop

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:57.390
wanted to make direct ignition,

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.158
they would first buy an original part,

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:00.760
drill a few holes in it,

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:01.961
and modify it to look like this.

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:02.595
So

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:04.197
how severe is this person's obsession?

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:05.565
Look at this

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:06.999
cross-section diagram AA.

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:07.967
This whole piece

00:06:07.967 --> 00:06:08.601
and this whole silver aluminum alloy

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:09.235
and this whole silver aluminum alloy

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:09.836
and this whole silver aluminum alloy

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:10.570
are all redrawn and redesigned by him.

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:11.637
After modification,

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:14.073
he

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:14.941
used a whole aluminum

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.175
ingot to CNC machine it and

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:16.776
then added it.

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:18.044
Of course, you might see it looking old

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.579
because he

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:21.481
had to test it halfway through the car's construction to see if it was OK.

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:21.914
If it's okay,

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.049
 

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:24.150
then

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.985
disassemble these things, organize them, and repaint them.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.453
Look at this carbon fiber tube; it 's a 3D

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:28.354
model.

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:30.590
What you see outside is

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:32.358
3D printing, then it's installed.

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:33.526
It's not 3D printed

00:06:33.526 --> 00:06:34.360
, tested

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:36.162
, and only after it meets the requirements is

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:38.064
it sent to a professional factory for further production.

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.499
That's back to what I just mentioned,

00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:40.666
the so-called OEM

00:06:40.666 --> 00:06:41.467
Level 2

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.435
prototyping. After that

00:06:42.435 --> 00:06:43.736
, those professional factories

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.671
hand it over to the original factory technicians

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:46.406
for further work.

00:06:46.406 --> 00:06:47.607
So you see,

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:49.108
to modify this carbon fiber

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.543
, your original radiator

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:51.444
will interfere.

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:53.413
What would a lower-end tuning shop

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:54.447
do?

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:55.815
They would move the entire original radiator

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:56.716
to the left side,

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:58.184
and if they need to repair it,

00:06:58.184 --> 00:06:59.051
they would just remove it. No,

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:00.486
they would

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:02.588
remake the entire radiator to a new size

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.791
, find a radiator specialist,

00:07:04.791 --> 00:07:06.793
remake the fan

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:08.161
, and reinstall it.

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:09.028
So the

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:10.997
visual proportions have to be correct.

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:12.732
Therefore, all their modifications and processing

00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:14.367
are based on our

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:15.468
industrial foundation.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:16.803
You have to draw up a plan first.

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:18.271
Next time you encounter the same car model

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:19.071
or the same thing,

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:20.339
you can always find

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:21.107
a lot of information

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.074
because they race themselves. When

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:22.909
you drive a motorcycle and find a problem,

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:24.010
you'll have a basis for your judgment

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:25.611
, not just relying on the experience of a seasoned mechanic.

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:27.680
I remember how it was done last time.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.115
And look at this picture, is

00:07:29.115 --> 00:07:30.950
n't it a plumber's wiring diagram?

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.018
Have you ever seen

00:07:32.018 --> 00:07:33.653
anyone draw a wiring diagram like this

00:07:33.653 --> 00:07:35.588
when modifying a motorcycle? Usually, when a seasoned mechanic modifies a motorcycle,

00:07:35.588 --> 00:07:36.489
they just

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:37.323
roughly connect the wires

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:38.224
and measure them.

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:39.459
They're meticulous enough to

00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:40.760
specify the wiring standards.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.361
Let me put it in the simplest terms.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:44.297
Among the motorcycle mechanics in

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:45.765
our channel's audience,

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:46.499
who is

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:47.333
very confident

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:48.935
that they can draw this?

00:07:48.935 --> 00:07:50.069
Maybe some people will raise their hands.

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:51.270
Can you be

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.139
very confident that you

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:54.640
can mentally rehearse

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:55.475
the resistance

00:07:55.475 --> 00:07:56.442
and ohm values

00:07:56.442 --> 00:07:58.010
​​and the wiring

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.045
before

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:00.680
adding it to the modification parts

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.448
and finally getting certified?

00:08:02.448 --> 00:08:03.716
There are very few people who can

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:04.884
customize their own. The standard

00:08:04.884 --> 00:08:08.120
should still conform to the original factory standard. The

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:10.356
original factory technical manual will definitely

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:12.558
have the standards, such as how much voltage and power supply this system needs, how much return power it needs.

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:13.759
For

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:14.594
example

00:08:14.594 --> 00:08:16.062
,

00:08:16.062 --> 00:08:17.763
Mercedes

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:18.564
has been around for 140 years.

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:19.198
In the past 100 years

00:08:19.198 --> 00:08:20.700
, there haven't been many major leaps

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:23.369
in engine technology

00:08:23.369 --> 00:08:24.070
, but

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:24.937
computer systems

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:26.172
or electronic control systems

00:08:26.172 --> 00:08:27.540
have made great strides

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:28.908
in recent years.

00:08:28.908 --> 00:08:29.909
So, in order to monitor

00:08:29.909 --> 00:08:31.644
the electrical power of

00:08:31.644 --> 00:08:32.812
each component

00:08:32.812 --> 00:08:34.113
, you need a

00:08:34.113 --> 00:08:34.981
MoTeC

00:08:34.981 --> 00:08:36.082
to monitor it.

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:36.983
Usually, aftermarket parts are

00:08:36.983 --> 00:08:38.017
just

00:08:38.017 --> 00:08:38.985
about installing

00:08:38.985 --> 00:08:39.485
whatever

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:40.286
you want.

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:41.254
So, that's why

00:08:41.254 --> 00:08:42.655
some cars,

00:08:42.655 --> 00:08:43.956
after being modified, easily become unstable

00:08:43.956 --> 00:08:45.391
or... It's easy to replace something

00:08:45.391 --> 00:08:46.158
and then problems arise.

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:47.426
Have you all heard the saying that

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:48.628
