00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:57.763
If I were to explain this to

00:09:57.763 --> 00:09:58.598
someone more into cars

00:09:58.598 --> 00:09:59.198
or industrial machinery,

00:09:59.198 --> 00:10:00.399
let me put it this way:

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:01.233
when you

00:10:01.233 --> 00:10:03.035
modify an engine, you need to make the

00:10:03.035 --> 00:10:04.170
front-wheel drive driveshaft

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:05.771
identical on both sides. Why is it

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:06.572
identical? Do you know why

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:07.473
vehicle design

00:10:07.473 --> 00:10:08.240
is difficult? Because

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:09.241
when you move just one part

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:10.710
or component , you

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:11.978
have to change everything else.

00:10:11.978 --> 00:10:13.145
It inevitably involves modifying

00:10:13.145 --> 00:10:14.413
many things,

00:10:14.413 --> 00:10:16.282
including the driveshaft.

00:10:16.282 --> 00:10:17.216
So, how do you make

00:10:17.216 --> 00:10:19.185
the driveshaft identical? If the driveshafts are different

00:10:19.185 --> 00:10:20.186
, even a slight difference on one

00:10:20.186 --> 00:10:21.387
side will cause it to veer to one side during

00:10:21.387 --> 00:10:22.955
straight-line acceleration

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:24.957
... That's the key point:

00:10:24.957 --> 00:10:26.292
the outer sides must be identical

00:10:26.292 --> 00:10:26.759
. Even

00:10:26.759 --> 00:10:28.427
the boss doesn't understand. Now

00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:30.262
